# Backend Folder Structure Rules

## Root Structure
```
/src
  /config          # Application configuration
  /models          # Database models
  /controllers     # Route controllers
  /middleware      # Express middleware
  /routes          # API routes
  /services        # Business logic
  /utils           # Helper functions and utilities
  /types           # TypeScript type definitions
  server.ts        # Entry point
```

## Service-Based Organization

Each domain service should have its own files within the respective folders:

### Models
```
/models
  /user
    user.model.ts
  /product
    product.model.ts
  /order
    order.model.ts
```

### Controllers
```
/controllers
  /user
    user.controller.ts
  /product
    product.controller.ts
  /order
    order.controller.ts
```

### Middleware
```
/middleware
  /auth
    auth.middleware.ts
  /validation
    validation.middleware.ts
  /error
    error.middleware.ts
```

### Routes
```
/routes
  /user
    user.routes.ts
  /product
    product.routes.ts
  /order
    order.routes.ts
  index.ts         # Route aggregator
```

### Services
```
/services
  /user
    user.service.ts
  /product
    product.service.ts
  /order
    order.service.ts
```

## Naming Conventions

- Files: Use kebab-case for multi-word filenames
- File suffixes should indicate the type: `.model.ts`, `.controller.ts`, `.middleware.ts`, etc.
- Classes: Use PascalCase (e.g., `UserModel`, `AuthMiddleware`)
- Functions/methods: Use camelCase (e.g., `getUserById`, `validateToken`)
- Interfaces/Types: Use PascalCase with prefix I for interfaces (e.g., `IUser`, `IProduct`)

## Import Rules

- Use relative paths for imports within a service
- Use absolute paths for cross-service imports (configure path aliases in tsconfig.json)
- Group imports: external dependencies first, then internal imports

## Code Organization

- Each file should have a single responsibility
- Related functionality should be grouped together in the same service

- Shared functionality should be moved to utils or dedicated services 